Description: A monitor that cannot show 3D shows the left eye whole
 Where a monitor cannot show a 3D video in 3D (Kdenlive runs on X11 under a
 compositor that takes stereo content on Wayland only, or the compositor
 refused the stereo declaration), it said so once and showed its frames as
 they are: in a 3D project the frame of two eyes in the monitor's area of one
 eye's shape, each eye squeezed to half its width, and in the clip monitor a
 3D clip's packed frame. A program never shows an eye squeezed (the stereo
 contract: "A program never stretches or squeezes an eye; KWin scales once, at
 the output"), so such a monitor now shows what Enable 3D off shows: the left
 eye of the 3D picture, whole and at its own shape, with nothing declared. The
 two sentences that tell the person say so ("It shows the left eye's view,
 flat."). Renders and thumbnails do not change.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-yet
Last-Update: 2026-11-22
